WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:05.859
Fans of That '70s Show probably noticed the
show's plot start to unravel in the second

00:00:05.859 --> 00:00:07.299
half of the series.

00:00:07.299 --> 00:00:11.799
For example, some may have noticed the years
on the license plates become inconsistent

00:00:11.799 --> 00:00:13.309
around season four.

00:00:13.309 --> 00:00:17.560
The first three seasons display a new year
starting in 1977.

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:22.660
After the fourth season, the years all stayed
the same, suggesting four seasons passing

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:26.930
in a single year, compared to the previous
four seasons in four years.

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:31.850
Perhaps the writers made the mistake of starting
a sitcom based in the '70s a little too late

00:00:31.850 --> 00:00:36.190
in the decade, and were forced to remain in
a single year for continuity reasons.

00:00:36.190 --> 00:00:41.550
However, superfans may remember there being
a Christmas episode every season, yet all

00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:45.370
of those Christmases would have had to occur
in a single year.

00:00:45.370 --> 00:00:49.420
Once fans started to think about some of the
plot holes in the later seasons, they may

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:54.079
have wondered if everything they saw on the
show was true or if something else was going

00:00:54.079 --> 00:00:56.090
on that fans weren't aware of.

00:00:56.090 --> 00:01:00.350
Some fans have taken this to the next level,
proposing a theory that might make a little

00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:01.410
too much sense.

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:05.890
Let’s check out the Eric theory that changes
everything on That '70s Show.

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:12.250
In Season 4 Episode 15, Tornado Prom, Eric
Foreman goes to prom with his group of stoner

00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:16.570
friends, but he forgets to bring his girlfriend,
Donna, who is stuck at the radio station where

00:01:16.570 --> 00:01:17.900
she works.

00:01:17.900 --> 00:01:21.790
This is a classic Foreman blunder that we’ve
come to expect from Eric.

00:01:21.790 --> 00:01:26.580
Being the lovable character he is, he decides
to rescue his stranded lady.

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:31.170
While doing so, a tornado is seen behind Eric's
car, but he doesn't notice it.

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:34.030
The episode goes on as usual, and the two
are reunited.

00:01:34.030 --> 00:01:38.260
They make it to prom and everything seems
great...at least on the surface.

00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:43.729
Some fans, especially at Entertainment Weekly,
took a deeper look at that episode and came

00:01:43.729 --> 00:01:47.450
up with a fan theory that would change everything
about the show.

00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:51.970
If you remember, while the prom is going on,
the parents of Eric and Donna are watching

00:01:51.970 --> 00:01:53.761
the news regarding the tornado when they hear:

00:01:53.761 --> 00:01:54.761
“This just in: the National Weather Service
has canceled the tornado warning.

00:01:54.761 --> 00:02:03.420
And updating our top story: a local teen is
in critical condition.”

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:07.470
You need a good ear to hear it, but the theory
goes that Eric Foreman never actually made

00:02:07.470 --> 00:02:08.539
it to Donna.

00:02:08.539 --> 00:02:13.209
Instead, the tornado caught up to Eric, who
is the local teen in critical condition.

00:02:13.209 --> 00:02:15.989
As a result, Eric falls into a coma.

00:02:15.989 --> 00:02:20.469
This would explain many of the inconsistencies
throughout the second half of the show.

00:02:20.469 --> 00:02:24.189
Let's say this was true; how would this have
affected the rest of the show?

00:02:24.189 --> 00:02:29.159
The theory is that since Eric is in a coma,
and not dead, the show continues based on

00:02:29.159 --> 00:02:33.439
his memory and how he believes certain situations
would unfold.

00:02:33.439 --> 00:02:38.310
For example, a few seasons later, Eric decides
to move to Africa to become a teacher.

00:02:38.310 --> 00:02:42.709
This is a little out of character for Eric,
but it also could mean that Eric was falling

00:02:42.709 --> 00:02:44.440
deeper into his coma.

00:02:44.440 --> 00:02:48.859
This could be something Eric always wanted
to do but couldn't because he'd always been

00:02:48.859 --> 00:02:50.379
stuck in Wisconsin.

00:02:50.379 --> 00:02:56.150
Following that, Eric is replaced by new character
Randy, who could be seen as Eric's imagined

00:02:56.150 --> 00:02:57.609
version of his older self.

00:02:57.609 --> 00:03:02.680
It could also mean he is falling even deeper
into his coma and losing perspective on what

00:03:02.680 --> 00:03:03.909
is plausible.

00:03:03.909 --> 00:03:09.489
This idea is bolstered even further when Fez
marries Jackie and Laurie on two separate

00:03:09.489 --> 00:03:10.609
occasions.

00:03:10.609 --> 00:03:15.900
Another example of fuzzy logic in later episodes
is when Eric's mom, Kitty, begins to record

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:18.030
everything that Eric is missing.

00:03:18.030 --> 00:03:21.699
This is potentially a way for Eric to stay
connected with what's going on at home while

00:03:21.699 --> 00:03:22.699
he is in the coma.

00:03:22.699 --> 00:03:27.070
None of this makes sense in the surface-level
plot, but Eric doesn't know that because he

00:03:27.070 --> 00:03:30.480
is drifting further and further away from
reality.

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:35.110
In the series finale, everyone is waiting
for Eric to return from Africa on New Year's

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:36.110
Eve.

00:03:36.110 --> 00:03:40.530
He does so in the last few minutes of the
show, and a warm-hearted reunion at a familiar

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:42.069
spot concludes the series.

00:03:42.069 --> 00:03:46.449
“I wish there was just some way to take
the edge off”

00:03:46.449 --> 00:03:49.909
“Edge, you are officially off”

00:03:49.909 --> 00:03:54.499
Of course, fans weren't satisfied with this
and had to work this event into their theory.

00:03:54.499 --> 00:04:00.930
Let's assume Eric was supposed to make a recovery
on December 31, 1979, when the show was supposed

00:04:00.930 --> 00:04:01.930
to end.

00:04:01.930 --> 00:04:06.049
The theory suggests that Eric doesn't make
it back home, that he is still in a coma,

00:04:06.049 --> 00:04:08.709
and that this is his last goodbye to everyone.

00:04:08.709 --> 00:04:14.079
His memory allows for one last time to remember
all of his friends and family back home.

00:04:14.079 --> 00:04:19.040
Then, when the series ends, that is when Eric
allegedly dies.

00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:23.410
It's a dark theory, but when you think about
it, it could make sense in the end.

00:04:23.410 --> 00:04:28.281
It's undeniable that there are several plot
holes in the later seasons, and maybe this

00:04:28.281 --> 00:04:33.500
could be explained by something like the main
character being struck by a tornado and falling

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:35.200
into a coma for a year.

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:37.470
Or maybe the writers just lost the plot.

00:04:37.470 --> 00:04:39.180
Perhaps we’ll never know!

